  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_4152fee4ccbd45c3b79c8f925ccc40ec",
      "statement": "The public entry point align_citations in src/cite_right/citations.py orchestrates a multi-step pipeline that segments the answer, prepares a PreparedCitationCorpus from the sources, selects candidate windows, runs Smith-Waterman to localize citations, ranks the survivors, runs the contradiction check, and assigns a per-span status; the public API surface (align_citations and PreparedCitationCorpus) is unchanged in 0.4.0.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:8267869be9c1dd05cc8ca65c96add4ca1ae2188c5c69db5a071c1afc351f21cf"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L72-L187",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f951b3e77d98a52114d2e7c251e6763abf4de2ebfeb7198c2bdaeaf08e58282e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9d4de5fcba7041a491cdb267d6f402e4",
      "statement": "On the default Rust path (SimpleTokenizer + SimpleSegmenter with cite_right._core importable) PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources delegates to _from_sources_rust, which uses rust_tokenize_and_prepare to build passage windows, IDF, and the inverted index in one Rust call, synchronizes the Python tokenizer's vocabulary from Rust, and keeps per-passage token data on the Rust PreparedCorpus for on-demand fetches; the candidate selector then calls rust_corpus.query_index for the conjunctive rare-token intersect, and Smith-Waterman still localizes each surviving candidate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1180-L1232",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e18b9435c09451ad7703bcd6bb8063ffcc95e181a0304c3020ac77b65daa476b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L126-L292",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eb8bc3d264d0e4082bf0e6ad4269b1818c1f8cee451dd5cc456b7ca2e6c75d11:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_36ea4def7eb74958933df268e26d5c26",
      "statement": "The fallback path runs when the Rust extension is missing or a custom tokenizer/segmenter is supplied: PreparedCitationCorpus.from_sources leaves inverted_index=None and rust_corpus=None on the corpus, the Python prepare path builds source passages and candidates with the SimpleTokenizer, and _select_candidates falls back to _add_lexical_candidates instead of the inverted-index intersect; Smith-Waterman still localizes via SmithWatermanAligner.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1220-L1228",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3cb953ef165bc3dbbaee1da579b46056813cdffb9e6642c3c27c428f00a7bf5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L126-L190",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8d2c530df4ff885b3461ca48d574ae56bbd77f733a5f5968df48af05ab689192:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53953fd5989f4b9b8f32682dcc4c9910",
      "statement": "When an embedder is provided, _add_embedding_candidates can add high-cosine-similarity windows to the candidate set even when they were not inverted-index seeds, and those non-index extras still need to be aligned by Smith-Waterman to become a Citation; lexical scores are filled only for inverted-index seeds, so embedding-only extras keep lexical_score == 0.0, retrieval_support is the channel for passages that the index or embedder selected but Smith-Waterman could not localize, and retrieval_support is not a Citation and never flips status. Rust prepare still runs in this case when SimpleTokenizer and SimpleSegmenter are in use; the 0.3.x skip of Rust prepare on the embedder path is gone.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1180-L1232",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e18b9435c09451ad7703bcd6bb8063ffcc95e181a0304c3020ac77b65daa476b:"
        },
