    {
      "id": "claim_d7057a5343604254b1ab0f821440b49f",
      "statement": "Both answer spans and source passages are tokenized with a single shared tokenizer instance (default SimpleTokenizer) that applies Unicode NFKC normalization and case-folding, and every token carries a (start_char, end_char) span in the original text so Smith-Waterman match positions can be re-expressed as character offsets in the source document; on the Rust prepare path the Python SimpleTokenizer's vocabulary is synchronized from rust_corpus.get_vocab() so answer-side tokens map to the same IDs as source-side tokens.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/prepared_corpus.py#L210-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0e828b9a0d5f60f701e9e1022735df025f4b91ab7902c9809e49e4ec53723d15:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/text/tokenizer.py#L66-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bd6cb88745f4d3a1e28502f294c360e38303047de8fe044c0e6a4f58a4f6f2da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_246810d7950b4c1fad7c36fc351419f0",
      "statement": "A citation is emitted from a candidate when the Smith-Waterman score clears min_alignment_score, the alignment token range is non-empty, and either the sequential answer coverage or the content-word coverage on the same passage clears min_answer_coverage; content-word coverage uses the tokenizer vocabulary to exclude stopwords, so a Smith-Waterman hit on only stopwords is not enough, and content-word overlap on the same candidate passage can emit a citation when sequential Smith-Waterman coverage is low so that grounded how-to and news paraphrases are not tagged \"unsupported\" just because shared content words are reordered.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L769-L782",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ee65f08a3559fdb90597cdfcc957a5a0e8df9ea8e2024379756014e35cd4a8c8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L785-L805",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b2d994ba7eb8cb1b5340067c352cb856502f3133365828f8727e5d51dd237309:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0852d07a836048a29804394851276101",
      "statement": "For structured field:value sources (Data2txt hours, amenities, business attributes) the pipeline runs a second Smith-Waterman pass per matching candidate with gap_score=0 on the answer text alone; faithful rewrites of hours, amenities, and similar fields can then be \"supported\" or \"partial\" while invented fields that do not match any field line stay \"unsupported\", and range dashes in fields are split into spaces so \"Monday-Friday\" tokenizes as two day names.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1040-L1102",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e0a7850c6ef6b49c369035b3f883f790dd73aa2b2738fae5160f44d67c5e9e6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L986-L1016",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:868a1020e52aac0733fcd2936e17687ddf83aca6ec96f212737453568a4f4350:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_74b27ed3216d45d69a2a8c1ba55b8810",
      "statement": "Citation char_start and char_end are absolute half-open character offsets into the source document, computed as the sum of the candidate source's base_doc_offset (for SourceChunk rebasing), the passage's doc_char_start/doc_char_end, and the token-level offset inside the passage; evidence is the slice of source text at that exact range, so source.text[citation.char_start:citation.char_end] == citation.evidence holds, and the same rebase logic is implemented by _slice_source_text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1376-L1381",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:381a97f49f96a995bb156510a3acf6588642911cb50acaa6424525e376b57be7:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1441-L1468",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ef179f5ef63d81e7c30c59b10691cc25c6fafad92acb14b518cfc94891bdcce4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0ff248e2e88648cf965da93bf7ee2bed",
      "statement": "Citations are ranked deterministically by -citation.score with tie-breaking that depends on prefer_source_order: when True the tie-break order is earlier source_index, then earlier char_start, then longer evidence span, then candidate_index; when False the order is earlier char_start, then longer evidence span, then source_index, then candidate_index; after sorting, citations from the same source with the same evidence-span tuple are deduped, max_citations_per_source caps per-source contributions, and the list is trimmed to top_k.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1523-L1550",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0941c75e7229f912c66590a2dc6339900ad275856f1c5643f833589af8453761:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1571-L1589",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7be18404e98e140082e00926d646303903b631097e54aca10b438e135a54dea4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_60f6a27d0f7e4d8eb9095f9749a44e74",
      "statement": "The contradiction check in src/cite_right/contradiction.py runs over the full candidate passage (via _contradiction_context), not the truncated Smith-Waterman evidence, and fires on negation mismatch, number mismatch, leftover n-gram slot mismatch (shared number attached to different content words), entity swap, and temporal/polarity marker pairs; when it fires against the best-ranked citation the span is downgraded to \"partial\" with citations and never to \"unsupported\", so source \"The vaccine is safe and effective.\" and answer \"The vaccine is not safe.\" resolves to \"partial\" with citations.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1592-L1632",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1090c77a209e9b5f7bad7e5480de6bc30f43058cb3de0f52a6709b37e91ebc0e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/contradiction.py#L67-L86",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f70aeaf2f9d9f4e2f042b29bb063e7ef3ba662211de4d1a1f39750ba682d6f09:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_375ae2f471de4a68a826d9444b1755c4",
      "statement": "Span status is one of exactly \"supported\", \"partial\", or \"unsupported\" and is assigned from the top-ranked Citation's answer_coverage component, not its overall score: \"supported\" requires answer_coverage >= supported_answer_coverage (default 0.6) and no contradiction fired, \"partial\" means citations exist but coverage is below threshold or contradiction fired, and \"unsupported\" means no citations survived filtering; the literal is \"partial\", never \"partially_supported\", and retrieval_support is intentionally outside the status decision.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L1610-L1633",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0546591f2ac5ef2ec8353fa6d983babe6920c357814b4eae7d76a64a8120f7ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/core/citation_config.py#L55-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2415ac4a547a7ce7eb1517a7a4aae4322d1ecd04b6e61a60764310d78f59a4c5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7c11542924c0402aa54932e98e30cec8",
      "statement": "The final citation score is a weighted sum of normalized_alignment, answer_coverage, evidence_coverage, lexical_score, and max(0, embedding_score) under CitationWeights (defaults: alignment=1.0, answer_coverage=1.0, evidence_coverage=0.0, lexical=0.5, embedding=0.5); per-citation components are also exposed on Citation.components for inspection and tuning.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/cite_right/citations.py#L808-L821",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:deb6b66ede4dfed1022481cea9c62b7d2836d8634ca663e0c0a63dcf9059d82a:"
        },
